<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_58f849907b52e99bd23af800f8d763a8229c9f259761916e6f9cd2caf9fafd1d_n0039/e_0010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SCD" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_58f849907b52e99bd23af800f8d763a8229c9f259761916e6f9cd2caf9fafd1d_n0039/e_0005/normalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/normalizationMappingStatus> "UNMAPPED" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_58f849907b52e99bd23af800f8d763a8229c9f259761916e6f9cd2caf9fafd1d_n0039/tu_0001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "1. In patients with NICM who either survive SCA due to VT/VF or experience hemodynamically unstable VT (LOE: B-R) (S7.2.1-1–S7.2.1-4) or stable sustained VT (LOE: B-NR) (S7.2.1-5) not due to reversible causes, an ICD is recommended if meaningful survival greater than 1 year is expected." .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_58f849907b52e99bd23af800f8d763a8229c9f259761916e6f9cd2caf9fafd1d_n0039/tu_0003> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "3. In patients with NICM who survive a cardiac arrest, have sustained VT, or have symptomatic VA who are ineligible for an ICD (due to a limited life-expectancy and/or functional status or lack of access to an ICD), amiodarone may be considered for prevention of SCD (S7.2.1-12,S7.2.1-13)." .
